  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 109 AM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nAs of 1 AM CDT, temperatures around the region are in the low to\nmid 50s with light winds. Fog has formed across far east central\nSD and is forecast to spread west into northeast SD and north\ninto west central MN through the rest of the early morning \nhours. This is expected to dissipate through the late morning.\n\nWe have a couple chances for showers through the second half of the \nweek. The first is late Thursday into early Friday morning as a cold \nfront moves across the region. The second is Saturday as a shortwave \nmoves across the area. Both events have chances less than 40%. \nThursday's precipitation will be concentrated over central SD with \naccumulations of more than a tenth of an inch at around or less than \n20%. Similar chances for Saturday, concentrated across northeast SD.\n\nHighs today will be 5 to 10 degrees above average before we sink \nbelow average Thursday through the weekend. Models are still showing \na slight warm up going into next work week. Still expecting stronger \nwind gusts Friday for areas west of the Missouri River, up to 30 \nmph, potentially up to 35 mph in south central SD. Wind gusts will \nalso be in the 25-35 mph range again Monday across most of the \nforecast area as high pressure gets pushed out by low pressure.",
